    {
      "id": "p0123-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In broad terms, Japan can be divided into two cultural halves, with Osaka representing western Japan and Tokyo representing eastern Japan. This division includes language, too - the Japanese dialect associated with Osaka sounds significantly different from the more \"standardized\" Tokyo dialect.",
        "raw": "In broad terms, Japan can be divided into two cultural halves, with Osaka\nrepresenting western Japan and Tokyo representing eastern Japan. This\ndivision includes language, too - the Japanese dialect associated with Osaka\nsounds significantly different from the more \"standardized\" Tokyo dialect.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.12136326,
          0.15664286,
          0.67974865,
          0.2204
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.11932062,
          0.15592857,
          0.68179129,
          0.22147143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "大致而言，日本文化可分为东西两部分，大阪代表西日本，东京代表东日本。语言也有这样的区分：大阪方言与较为“标准化”的东京方言，听起来有明显差异。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
